  "method_changes": [
    "Actual raw engine traversal supports independently parameterized custom container and value via unsafe projection traits.",
    "Calls custom Capacity once; cached end survives copying, conversion and Restart.",
    "Preserves native inner-block scan exceeding a custom short end, then exhausts to the captured end.",
    "Custom getItem dispatch occurs on every dereference/arrow, including field-offset projection from nonzero-position base storage.",
    "Same-specialization copy/assignment, mutable-to-const conversion/assignment, cross-const comparisons, prefix identity and fully mutable shallow postfix state.",
    "Unsafe item references enforce aliasing obligations of copied native cursors; raw mutable arrow creates no reference.",
    "No Clone bounds on container or value; default source projection and native beyond-end index semantics exercised."
  ],
  "remaining_partial_contracts": [
    "Typed SparseArray facade still uses its earlier BTreeMap storage and cursor implementation; delegation remains separate.",
    "Raw owning engine is Rc/UnsafeCell and not Send/Sync. Delegation must preserve existing typed auto-traits through explicit ownership/thread design.",
    "BasicIterator itself has no Value/ChangeValue methods in native OCCT; Rust value/change_value are access adapters corresponding to typed-wrapper usage and receive no invented BasicIterator declaration credit.",
    "Native typedef/algorithm trait correspondence and compiler-proven template instantiation closure remain pending; public methods are only ID-bound candidates here.",
    "Mutable iterator construction borrows the custom source readonly; actual write access requires unsafe writable-source projection/exclusive-reference guarantees. Native const-to-mutable conversion is intentionally unavailable.",
    "Structural invalidation and expired cursor access retain unsafe preconditions; Rust rejects detached projection via panic instead of claiming native undefined behavior equivalence."
  ],
